(This creature enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it. If X is 5 or more, draw a card when it enters.)\\nTrample\\nSpawn Termagants — Whenever Tervigon deals combat damage to a player, create that many 1/1 green Tyranid creature tokens.', 'Reach, deathtouch\\nHypertoxic Miasma — All lands have "{T}: Add one mana of any color" and lose all other abilities.', 'Relentless March — {X}, {T}, Tap X untapped artifacts you control: Target opponent loses X life.', "Return all attacking creatures to their owner's hand.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nFlashback—Sacrifice three creatures. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Reverberating Summons — At the beginning of your end step, each opponent loses 2 life. Then for each opponent who has less life than you, create a 1/3 black Demon creature token named Plaguebearer of Nurgle.', 'Rogue Trader — Whenever Neyam Shai Murad deals combat damage to a player, you may have that player return target permanent card from their graveyard to their hand. If you do, that player chooses a permanent card in your graveyard, then you put it onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Rugged Highlands enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rugged Highlands enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Scoured Barrens enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Scoured Barrens enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Search your library for a Plains, Island, Swamp, or Mountain card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for an artifact card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the other into your hand, then shuffle.', "Secrets of the Soul — {T}, Sacrifice another creature: Add an amount of {B} equal to the sacrificed creature's mana value.", 'Sorcerous Inspiration — At the beginning of your upkeep, return an instant or sorcery card at random from your graveyard to your hand.\\nFire of Tzeentch — Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Exalted Flamer of Tzeentch deals 1 damage to each opponent.', 'Spiritual Leader — At the beginning of combat on your turn, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nPsychic Stimulus — {T}: Add {C}{C}. When you next cast a spell with {X} in its mana cost or activate an ability with {X} in its activation cost this turn, copy that spell or ability. You may choose new targets for the copy. (A copy of a permanent spell becomes a token.)', "Squad {2} (As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {2} any number of times. When this creature enters the battlefield, create that many tokens that are copies of it.)\\nArco-Flagellant can't block.\\nEndurant — Pay 3 life: Arco-Flagellant gains indestructible until end of turn.", "Squad {2} (As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {2} any number of times. When this creature enters the battlefield, create that many tokens that are copies of it.)\\nFlying, vigilance\\nMiracle {1}{W} (You may cast this card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)", 'Squad {2} (As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {2} any number of times. When this creature enters the battlefield, create that many tokens that are copies of it.)\\nFlying\\nSuppressing Fire — Whenever Vanguard Suppressor deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Squad {2} (As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {2} any number of times. When this creature enters the battlefield, create that many tokens that are copies of it.)\\nGrav-cannon — When Space Marine Devastator enters the battlefield, destroy up to one target artifact or enchantment.', 'Squad {2} (As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {2} any number of times. When this creature enters the battlefield, create that many tokens that are copies of it.)\\nOther creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Starstorm deals X damage to each creature.\\nCycling {3} ({3}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Stowage — Whenever Goliath Truck attacks, put two +1/+1 counters on another target attacking creature.\\nCrew 2 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 2 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'Strategic Coordinator — Basic lands you control have "{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only on costs that contain {X}."', 'Strive — This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nUntil end of turn, any number of target creatures each gain "Whenever this creature attacks, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token that\'s tapped and attacking."', "Subterranean Assault — Whenever Trygon Prime attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it and a +1/+1 counter on up to one other target attacking creature. That creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'Swiftwater Cliffs enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Swiftwater Cliffs enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature get -3/-3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn for each Swamp you control.', "Target player sacrifices an attacking creature. You create X 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens, where X is that creature's toughness.", 'Targeting Relay — At the beginning of combat on your turn, choose an opponent.\\nCreatures attacking the last chosen player have menace.', 'Temple of Abandon enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Abandon enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'The first creature spell you cast each turn costs {2} less to cast.\\nWhenever an opponent casts their first noncreature spell each turn, Shadow in the Warp deals 2 damage to that player.', "The owner of target permanent shuffles it into their library, then reveals the top card of their library. If it's a permanent card, they put it onto the battlefield.", 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature on the battlefield.\\nBlasphemous Act deals 13 damage to each creature.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature that died this turn.\\nDiscard your hand, then draw eight cards. Blood for the Blood God! deals 8 damage to each opponent. Exile Blood for the Blood God!', 'Thornwood Falls enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Thornwood Falls enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Tomb Fortress enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\n{2}{B}{B}{B}, {T}, Exile Tomb Fortress: Mill four cards, then return a creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Trample, haste\\nSkilled Outrider — Whenever Atalan Jackal deals combat damage to a player, you may search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Trample\\nBattle Cannon — When Chaos Defiler enters the battlefield or dies, for each opponent, choose a nonland permanent that player controls. Destroy one of them chosen at random.', 'Trample\\nBio-Plasmic Scream — Whenever you cast a creature spell with mana value 5 or greater, Screamer-Killer deals 5 damage to any target.', 'Trample\\nDevastating Charge — Other creatures you control have trample.', 'Trample\\nFrenzied Rampage — At the beginning of combat on your turn, choose an opponent at random. Knight Rampager attacks that player this combat if able.\\nWhen Knight Rampager dies, it deals 4 damage to target opponent chosen at random.', 'Trample\\nMark of Chaos Ascendant — During your turn, spells you cast from your hand with mana value X or less have cascade, where X is the total amount of life your opponents have lost this turn.', 'Trample\\nOther creatures you control have trample.\\nWhen Old One Eye enters the battlefield, create a 5/5 green Tyranid creature token.\\nFast Healing — At the beginning of your precombat main phase, you may discard two cards. If you do, return Old One Eye from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Trample\\nRapid-fire Battle Cannon — When Knight Paladin enters the battlefield, it deals 4 damage to each opponent.\\nCrew 1 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 1 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'Trample\\nWarp Vortex — When Mutalith Vortex Beast enters the battlefield, flip a coin for each opponent you have. For each flip you win, draw a card. For each flip you lose, Mutalith Vortex Beast deals 3 damage to that player.', 'Tranquil Cove enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Tranquil Cove enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Ultima Founding — {T}, Tap two untapped artifacts you control: Create a 2/2 white Astartes Warrior creature token with vigilance.\\nMaster of Machines — {T}, Tap X untapped creatures you control: Look at the top X cards of your library. You may reveal an artifact card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'Veil of Time — Whenever Epistolary Librarian attacks, you may cast a spell with mana value X or less from your hand without paying its mana cost, where X is the number of attacking creatures.', 'Vigilance\\nExile Cannon — When Canoptek Tomb Sentinel enters the battlefield from a graveyard, exile up to one target nonland permanent.\\nUnearth {7} ({7}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', 'Vigilance\\nUnquestionable Wisdom — Other creatures you control get +1/+0 and have vigilance.\\nHunt for Heresy — {1}, {T}: Tap target creature an opponent controls. Investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', 'Void Shields — Protection from mana value 3 or less\\nGatling Blaster — Whenever Reaver Titan attacks, it deals 5 damage to each opponent.\\nCrew 4 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 4 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)', 'Ward {2} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {2}.)\\nThree Autostubs — Whenever another source you control deals exactly 1 damage to a permanent or player, Ghyrson Starn, Kelermorph deals 2 damage to that permanent or player.', 'When Defenders of Humanity enters the battlefield, create X 2/2 white Astartes Warrior creature tokens with vigilance.\\n{X}{2}{W}, Exile Defenders of Humanity: Create X 2/2 white Astartes Warrior creature tokens with vigilance. Activate only if you control no creatures and only during your turn.', 'When Primaris Eliminator enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Executioner Round — Destroy target creature.\\n• Hyperfrag Round — Creatures target player controls get -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'When Technomancer enters the battlefield, mill three cards, then return any number of artifact creature cards with total mana value 6 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'When The Flesh Is Weak enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.\\nCreatures you control with +1/+1 counters on them are artifacts in addition to their other types.\\nNonartifact creatures get -1/-1.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, it deals damage equal to its power to any target.', 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, put X +1/+1 counters on target creature you control, where X is the power of the creature that died.', 'Whenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control from anywhere other than your hand or you cast a spell from anywhere other than your hand, create a 3/3 red Spawn creature token.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, put four +1/+1 counters on it.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, you may draw two cards. If you do, discard a card.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Worn Powerstone enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}{C}.', "Wraith Form — Canoptek Wraith can't be blocked.\\nTransdimensional Scout — When Canoptek Wraith deals combat damage to a player, you may pay {3} and sacrifice it. If you do, choose a land you control. Then search your library for up to two basic land cards which have the same name as the chosen land, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'You may have Sculpting Steel enter the battlefield as a copy of any artifact on the battlefield.', 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may cast artifact spells and colorless spells from the top of your library.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Exile the top card of your library.', 'You may play an additional land this turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'You may reveal the first card you draw each turn as you draw it. Whenever you reveal an instant or sorcery card this way, create Cherubael, a legendary 4/4 black Demon creature token with flying.\\nWhenever Inquisitor Eisenhorn deals combat damage to a player, investigate that many times. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{U}.', '{1}{B}, {T}: Choose another target artifact creature you control. When that creature dies this turn, return it to the battlefield tapped under your control.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wayfarer's Bauble: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", '{2}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you control three or more lands with the same name.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Add three mana of any one color. Activate only if you control three or more lands with the same name.', '{T}: Add three mana of any one color.', '{T}: Add {B}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity. If you spend this mana to cast your commander, it enters the battlefield with a number of additional +1/+1 counters on it equal to the number of times it's been cast from the command zone this game.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{4}, {T}, Sacrifice Cave of Temptation: Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a storage counter on Molten Slagheap.\\n{1}, Remove X storage counters from Molten Slagheap: Add X mana in any combination of {B} and/or {R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Unstable Obelisk: Destroy target permanent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Talisman of Indulgence deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Talisman of Dominance deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Talisman of Creativity deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Talisman of Hierarchy deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Talisman of Progress deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Hedron Archive: Draw two cards.']
flavor: ['"Agresto, bring up the rear . . . Agresto?"\\n—Sergeant Dremark Eigen, last words', '"Any Cadian who can\'t field-strip their own lasgun by age ten was born on the wrong planet."\\n—Anonymous', '"As Horus once besieged the Sol System, we shall bring the rotting Imperium to its knees."\\n—Abaddon the Despoiler', '"As swift as a lash mamba, as sharp as a spineleaf, as stubborn as a wild grox."\\n—Colonel Pannet, in praise of the Catachan warrior', '"Aza\'gorod, the Nightbringer. The embodiment of death. A killer of stars and of worlds."\\n—Illuminor Szeras', '"Bolters, flamers, plasma—we hit the xenos with everything, and it just kept coming."\\n—Captain Uriel Ventris', '"Bolters? Chainswords? All fine weapons, however I wield a far more dangerous power."', '"By this oath, I pledge to stand by thee, against traitor, beast, or fiend, for only in death does duty end."', '"Charge brothers! Death to the false Emperor!"', '"Embrace the strength of your Primarch, but deny the Red Thirst, brothers! There is no return from that darkest of paths."', '"Embrace your hunger, your lust, your desire. The universe is ours for the taking!"\\n—Sanctifer LeVay, Cult of the Sacred Union', '"Engaging Protector protocol."', '"Hail the Children of the Stars!"\\n—Magus Lucea Kane', '"Hold your bitterness deep within, and there let it fester. Let it roil and squirm and churn, until you are filled with bile so poisonous that all you touch falls to ruin."\\n—Mortarion, Daemon Primarch', '"Hunger is no different from any other foe; defeat it in the Emperor\'s name, and save Humanity."\\n—Motto of the Agri-World Viridia IV', '"I am the Arch-fiend, the Despoiler of Worlds, and by my hands shall the false Emperor fall."\\n—Abaddon the Despoiler', '"I can show you indulgence without regret, delight without boundaries, gratifications beyond count."\\n—Sha\'ris, Deacon of Lust', '"I shall seek the Emperor\'s forgiveness in the darkest places of the night."\\n—Oath of the Penitent', '"Immortality is not quite the same as invulnerability, but it is close enough."', '"In the embrace of the great Nurgle, I am no longer afraid, for with His pestilential favour I have become that which I once most feared: Death."\\n—Kulvain Hestarius of the Death Guard', '"It appears Old One Eye is on the hunt."\\n—Marneus Calgar', '"It is my cry that wakes you in the night, and my body that crouches in the shadow. I am Tzeentch and you are the puppet that dances to my tune."\\n—*The Book of Tzeentch*', '"It is their duty to fight and die so that Humanity might be preserved."\\n—Lord Commissar Barron Reed', '"It\'s a lifeless ruin of some long-lost race. What is there to fear?"\\n—Commissar Gadholm', '"Let the others bicker over their little worlds and stars. I have an empire of knowledge, and it encompasses all others."\\n—Trazyn the Infinite', '"Looks like we\'ve found the source. Torch it quick, before anything crawls out."\\n—Sergeant "Ripper" Jackson', '"My Master is the Beginning and he is the End. He is the Master of Mortals, and the core of our Dead Hearts."\\n—*The Saga of Khorne*', '"No. No! Not the sarcophagus . . . Khorne damn you, you disloyal curs. JUST KILL ME!"\\n—Kalos the Ravager', '"Nothing clears a battlefield like a Deathstrike missile. Wait. Is something moving out there?"\\n—Commander Zander At\'lan, Tallarn 115th Armoured Regiment', '"Now!"', '"Of all the stars in the Galaxy, Sol is of the Emperor. Its heat is His might. Its light is His revelation."\\n—*Lectitio Divinitatus*', '"Once we have claimed this planet, we will claim the stars."', '"Once, the C\'tan sought to rule us. Now it is they who serve us, their shards powering our great machines."\\n—Szarekh, the Silent King', '"One day, the dark glory of the void will swallow the light of the stars once and for all!"\\n—Magus Lucea Kane', '"Only the deathless can truly comprehend the burden of unfailing loyalty."\\n—Vargard Obyron of the Sautekh Dynasty', '"Our will shall be our weapons, our faith shall be our armour."\\n—Canticle of Absolution', '"Ours is to honour the martyr, tend the fallen, defend the innocent, and walk always in the light."\\n—*The Hospitaller\'s Book of Hours*', '"Pain is an ally. Pain is a friend. Pain is truth."\\n—Sister Erynica N\'botu, Order of the Valorous Heart', '"Power comes in many shapes. But real power does the shaping."\\n—Abaddon the Despoiler', '"Praise Nurgle! For the plague to have progressed so quickly, truly his blessing must be upon us!"\\n—Ku\'gath Plaguefather', '"Pray that night is upon us, for if this twilight is the work of the Necrons, we are all dead men."\\n—Address by Lieutenant Krakos prior to the Bloodmoon Massacres', '"Rise and serve me once more."\\n—Trazyn the Infinite', '"Scour this world of these impudent trespassers!"\\n—Lord Traedrekkh of the Sekemtar Dynasty', '"See that cloud that hangs around it? More than a minute in there and you\'ll be bleeding out of places you didn\'t even know you had."\\n—Captain Ascote', '"Some may question your right to destroy ten billion people. Those who understand know that you have no right to let them live."\\n—Exterminatus Extremis', '"Target eradicated. That which burns shall ever be blessed."\\n—Fusilave unit Tor-213', '"That which was, will be. That which will be, was."\\n—Kairos Fateweaver', '"The ancient Necron race has achieved this pinnacle of elegance through their relentless pursuit of utility."\\n—Tech-Priest Darvin, executed for heresy 1256998.M41', '"The star-born approach! Their holy angels descend! Take up arms, my brothers and sisters, for the Day of Ascension is upon us!"', '"The war will be decided here, where the planet\'s defences are strongest."\\n—Marneus Calgar', '"They are my bulwark against the Terror. They are the Defenders of Humanity. They are my Space Marines."\\n—The Emperor of Mankind', '"They\'re beasts! What are they going to do, bomb us from orbit?"\\n—Platoon Commander Cyrus Jalili, Prandium Defence Auxilia', '"This cogitator provides a strategic overview of the battlefield. By which I mean, of course, the entire planet."', '"This galaxy once knelt before us, and it will do so again."', '"This heresy cannot stand!"', '"This sword has many names. You may call it \'Death.\'"\\n—Kaldor Draigo, Supreme Grand Master of the Grey Knights', '"Though it may take an eternity, I will see the myriad dynasties united once more."', '"Tzeentch cares not what they were or what they become. Only that they change."\\n—Kairos Fateweaver', '"We guarantee you that within a week, you will feel like a new man."\\n—Galaxos Klynesmith, biophagus', '"We shall wage this war with undaunted faith and courage. We shall not take one step back."\\n—Lord Marshal Toshenko to the Vostroyan 16th', '"We\'ve reached the xenos HQ. Transmitting coordinates now."', '"What are ramparts, what are steeples, what are our machines worth in the teeth of this ceaseless hunger?"\\n—Magos Varnak', '"When the Silent King saw what had been done, he knew at last the true nature of the C\'tan, and the doom they had wrought in his name."\\n—*The Book of Mournful Night*', '"When the door drops, give them a taste of the Emperor\'s fire!"\\n—Commissar Yarrick', '"While we slept, our inferiors infested the worlds that belong to us. Now, we awaken once more."\\n—Szarekh, the Silent King', '"Witchcraft or technology, it is blasphemous, and it must be stopped."\\n—Inquisitor Greyfax', '"You mortals turn to dust in the blink of an eye. I only expedite your fate."', 'A foe without honour is a foe already beaten.', "A hive tyrant's synaptic link is the primary conduit through which the Hive Mind enforces its dominance over a hive fleet's lesser creatures.", 'A single spore from a Tyranid Hive Ship can spell doom for a solar system.', 'Abandoned tunnels and bunkers below the hive city have been secretly recolonized and dubbed the "Forbidden Cities."', 'All Necrons bear the mark of the Triarch, a brand upon their living-metal skin that binds them to their dynasty.', 'All orbital bombardment did was till the soil.', 'Anrakyr the Traveller awoke from his slumber with a singular goal: to rebuild a united Necron galaxy.', 'Armageddon has become a site of holy pilgrimage for the Orks: a planet where the fighting never stops.', 'As part of their indoctrination and training, a psyker learns to focus their mental strength through a psycho-reactive staff.', 'As the continent sank over the course of eons, the tomb complex slowly flooded. The sleeping Necrons, their stasis crypts corrupted, never awoke.', "As the fusillade of lasgun fire bounced harmlessly off the carnifex's carapace, the creature roared and advanced.", "At the lash of the hive ship's feeder tentacles, the cruiser vented atmosphere, cargo, and crew members into the void.", 'Before the Great Sleep, the Necrons knew every corner of the galaxy, as only the ultimate conquerors could.', 'Blight grenades—which induce horrendous effects on their victims—have no impact on the Death Guard, who gladly use the devices in extreme close quarters with the enemy.', 'Bound to a cryptek, the cryptothrall exists for one reason: to defend its master to the death.', 'By the physical laws of our universe, darkness is merely the absence of light. Necrons can harness the power of other dimensions, where darkness is tangible and moldable.', 'By the time the Blood Angels descended from the heavens, Phodia was a city transformed. Miles of flesh-filled rivers fed into the central digestion pools and up into the hive fleet above.', "Centuries' worth of black iron lie beneath the soil of every Imperial world, their civilization built on never-ending strife.", 'Chaos renegades always seek to deface and destroy effigies of Imperial piety, replacing them with blasphemous symbols of the Ruinous Powers.', 'Charged with psychic energy, the melee weapons of the Tyranid are far more than bone and chitin.', 'Countless xenos cults dwell unseen within the Imperium, lurking just beneath the surface.', 'Created to break will and bone with equal ferocity.', 'Deep-space ports provide temporary shelter for Imperial cruisers on long voyages.', 'Defence laser emplacements are usually located at high altitude, where the rarified air does little to impede their range of destructive efficacy.', 'Deserts of industrial ash surround the hive cities, covering the surface of the planet with an unstable, corrosive skin.', "Disillusioned with the Imperium, the population of Chancer's Vale turned to other, hungrier powers for meaning.", 'During biotransference, the Necrontyr lost almost all individuality. What little remained was imprisoned within a living metal form.', "Each plaguebearer is formed from the blighted soul of a mortal slain by Nurgle's Rot.", "Every kill is a sacrament of the Emperor's glory.", 'Genestealer Cults bide their time on Imperial worlds, spreading tendrils of corruption through the native population.', 'Harrowing visions, paralyzing pain, and terrifying brain spasms await those who challenge the cult.', 'Heretic cultists came to the planet Sovereign in search of resources and precious artifacts. They found something else.', "High-ranking plaguebearers of Nurgle's realm ride into realspace mounted upon Rot Flies—colossal daemonic insects whose appearance is so repugnant it scars the mind.", "In its attempts to mirror Tzeentch's convoluted scheming, the Crystal Labyrinth constantly shifts and rearranges itself.", 'In the hearts of mortals, in the pages of ancient lore, in the deep, forgotten places of the universe . . . Chaos waits.', "In the late stages of a Tyranid invasion, sessile organisms take root in a planet's crust, converting its resources into biomass that can be extracted by the Hive Fleet.", 'In the late stages of a Tyranid invasion, vast capillary towers funnel biomass to the Hive Ships waiting in orbit.', 'In the roiling depths of the Eye of Terror, the bloodthirsty hordes of Chaos Marines plot the downfall of their loyalist brethren.', "It burns with the very fire that doomed Szarekh's species, and channels it to devastate his foes.", 'It emits a stinking cloud composed of millions of nascent microscopic organisms, each possessing a fragment of predatory sentience.', 'Its shriek is unintelligible, but armored bulkheads seem to understand the intent well enough.', "Khorne's sole desire is to drown the galaxy in a tide of slaughter. To conquer and kill every living thing, until there is nothing left but spilled blood and shattered bone.", 'Masters of dimensional dissonance, singularity manipulation, and countless other technologies, plasmancers are terrifying to behold.', 'Mere weeks later, the planet was scoured of any trace of life. Every scrap of vegetation, every drop of water—gone.', 'Millennia of constant warfare have left many planets with very little worth fighting over.', 'Most denizens of an Imperial hive city live and die without ever setting foot inside the towering skyscrapers of the ruling class.', 'Necrodermis, the living metal from which all Necrons are made, is endlessly adaptive.', 'No berzerker charge can stand against the psychic might of the Hive Mind.', 'Nothing can override the hard-wired desire to kill that empowers these rage-driven Necrons.', 'On countless frontier worlds, below silica sand, blasted chalk, or bubbling marsh, slumbering Necrons wait.', 'On the Planet of Sorcerers in the Eye of Terror lies the Tower of the Cyclops, the redoubt of Magnus the Red.', 'Only the most pious and devoted Imperial servants are granted the posthumous honor of becoming servo-skulls.', 'Places of worship become frenzies of violence as the psychic call of the Hive Mind stirs Genestealer Cults to action.', 'Poxwalkers are victims of the Walking Pox, a cruel virulence which rots the infected to death while keeping them conscious.', 'Skulls for the Skull Throne.', 'Stripped and blasted by millennia of war, every planet eventually looks the same.', 'The Archaeovist of the Solemnace Galleries will not rest until every treasure in the galaxy is safely within his clutches.', 'The Battle of Baal was the bloodiest and most costly in the entire noble history of the Sons of Sanguinius.', 'The Brazen Thunder, foremost of the bloodcrusher legions, are named for the sound they make as they ride into battle.', 'The Changer of Ways often sends glimpses of possible futures to his most loyal acolytes, visions that would destroy lesser minds.', "The Chapter's honored dead are interred in the Hall of Heroes, where the mineral-rich water of the catacombs slowly fossilizes their bones, preserving them for all time.", 'The Cicatrix Maledictum split the galaxy asunder. The raw stuff of Chaos flooded into realspace, transforming whole planets in moments.', 'The Emperor is the greatest psyker in Human history. For thousands of years, he has sat immobile in a palace that spans a continent.', 'The Genestealer Cults rejoiced at the arrival of their gods . . . at first.', "The Imperium's most peaceful worlds serve only to arm and supply the others.", "The Lords of Change are Tzeentch's greatest servants. The most powerful of them wield fragments of his power over destiny.", 'The Tyranids advance inexorably across the galaxy in their living Hive Ships, with one singular goal: to consume all.', "The arcane sphere that hovers near Magnus's staff imbues it with the power to transform enemies into mindless chaos spawn.", 'The astropath collapsed, his empty eye sockets aglow. He spoke three words before falling lifeless to the ground: "They . . . are . . . coming!"', 'The battle began with an overwhelming wave of Tyranids and ended with Canoness Lucretia standing atop a huge pile of charred alien corpses.', 'The blessed union of gun, claw, and merciless intent is a force to be truly feared.', 'The flesh of the Necrontyr is a memory so distant as to be nearly mythical.', 'The gods of Chaos bestow gifts of mutations upon their champions. Too many of these gifts transform their bearer into mindless, writhing chaos spawn.', 'The practice of tracking and training Thunderwolves is a sort of initiation ritual into the upper echelons of the Wolf Guard.', 'The squad plunged deep into Hive Pandorial, finding only the shambling corpses of those they came to avenge.', 'The vaults of the Necron Dynasties contain all manner of esoteric artifacts, most forged long before many of the younger races even existed.', 'The voice of a clamavus commands all who carry the genetic legacy of the Tyranids in their blood.', 'The walls of the Necron tomb were unbreakable. The ground beneath it was not.', 'The weapons deployed to drive the Traitor Legions into the Eye of Terror were so destructive that some planets still have not recovered.', 'There are those who draw false comparisons between the tech-magi of the Adeptus Mechanicus and the xenotechnologists of the necron race. There can be no mercy for such heretics.', 'There is no greater bulwark than the Praetors of the Adeptus Custodes, the bodyguards of the Emperor of Mankind.', 'They all took up the cry, the missionaries, the pilgrims, the sisters of the Orders Militant. The forces of Chaos melted before the fire of their faith.', 'They dive screaming on defensive lines, sowing chaos before the main assault begins.', 'Those suspected of carrying the flayer curse are summarily banished, lest the corruption spread to other Necrons.', "Through blood and battle, scouts are forged from raw recruits into the Imperium's finest.", 'To look upon one is to surrender every last shred of self-will.', 'Too obviously xenos in form to blend into human society, the acolytes haunt the dark places beneath industrial sprawls.', 'Tyranids flourish in any climate, dominate any ecosystem, crush any resistance.', "Tzeentch's beastmen twist reality as they themselves are twisted.", 'Under his rule, there is but one creed: Chaos shall reign.', "Upon impact with a planet's surface, a tyrannocyte's bloated belly bursts open, disgorging a horde of Tyranid invaders.", 'Used carefully, material that has been exposed to the baleful energies of the Warp can be contained to fuel powerful rituals.', "War is a dance. And they're looking for partners.", "When Chaos makes a tool that isn't specifically for destroying things, it's usually for finding new things to destroy.", 'When the Great Rift opened across the Galaxy, many Imperial worlds were lost to Chaos.', 'With each defeat, the hive learns. With each victory, it grows.', 'Within it rests the power of a sun, and none of the warmth.']
artist: ['Aaron J. Riley', 'Adrián Rodríguez Pérez', 'Alex Konstad', 'Alexander Mokhov', 'Alexey Kruglov', 'Andrey Nyarl', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Devine', 'Anton Solovianchyk', 'Antonio José Manzanedo', 'Artur Nakhodkin', 'Bartek Fedyczak', 'Billy Christian', 'Bryan Sola', 'Calder Moore', 'Cory Trego-Erdner', 'Daarken', 'Darren Tan', 'David Astruga', 'David Auden Nash', 'David Sondered', 'David Álvarez', 'Diego Gisbert', 'Eliz Roxs', 'Evan Shipard', 'Fajareka Setiawan', 'Filipe Pagliuso', 'Games Workshop', 'Hector Ortiz', 'Helge C. Balzer', 'Henry Peters', 'Heonhwa Choe', 'Irina Nordsol', 'Ivan Dedov', 'JB Casacop', 'Jake Murray', 'Johan Grenier', 'Johannes Mücke', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Josu Solano', 'Kamila Szutenberg', 'Kekai Kotaki', 'Kim Sokol', 'L J Koh', 'Lie Setiawan', 'Lixin Yin', 'Logan Feliciano', 'Lucas Terryn', 'Marina Ortega Lorente', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Michał Miłkowski', 'Miguel Sacristan', 'Mirko Failoni', 'Nikola Matkovic', 'Oleg Shekhovtsov', 'Philip Helliwell', 'Pierre Loyvet', 'Rafater', 'Roman Tishenin', 'Sergei Leoluch Panin', 'Sergio Cosmai', 'Seseon Yoon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stanton Feng', 'Steve Argyle', 'Teodora Dumitriu', 'Wisnu Tan', 'Wonchun Choi', 'Xavier Ribeiro', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zhillustrator', 'Álvaro Calvo Escudero', 'Ørjan Ruttenborg Svendsen']
